      "math_academy_id": "q-40413",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{span}\\{b\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-5)+(-2)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-2-6+2}{4+4+4+4}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-16}{16}b \\\\  & =-b \\\\  & =-1[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
